  practises: "Decoding by sounding out and blending, and checking meaning instead of guessing from the picture. Pictures appear only after the child has had time to read.",
  levels: [["1 · Beacon (5–6)", "CVC words, sound buttons on; 3 pictures"], ["2 · Beacon (5–6)", "CCVC / CVCC words and 2 exception words (the, I)"], ["3 · Beacon (6–7)", "Short sentences: 'The pig is in the mud.'"], ["4 · Beacon (6–7)", "Sense or silly? 'The cup can run.' goes to the silly shed"]],
  feedback: "Right: the carriage couples and the train toots, then the word is read aloud. First miss: \"Good guess, but try again\" and sound buttons pulse. Second: the word is sounded out slowly. Pictures arrive after a short 'read first' pause so the child reads instead of guessing.",
  rationale: "The read-first pause and silly-sentence check target the source's 'stop-and-think (not guessing)' goal.",
  transfer: "Reading labels and signs aloud; 'sense or silly' sentence games with an adult.",
  a11y: ["Sound buttons under every grapheme", "Font size adjustable; dyslexia-friendly spacing option", "Read-first pause adjustable by adults"],
  visuals: ["Railway through hills", "Otto in the cab", "Word engine", "Picture carriages", "Silly shed", "Station board of words read"],
  reward: { icon: "🚂", name: "A long train of words" },
