  does: "The child is a puppet in Mabel's play. They hear the line read well (Listen), read it together with the highlight (Together), then read it alone (My turn) while the phrase highlight moves at their chosen pace. A quick question checks they followed the scene.",
  practises: "Reading the same short text several times in phrases, the 'listen, together, alone' sequence, then checking understanding.",
  levels: [["1 · Beacon (6–7)", "One-line parts, phrase highlight on, slow pace"], ["2 · Beacon (6–7)", "Two-line parts with a question mark or exclamation (expression)"], ["3 · Lighthouse (7–8)", "Short scene, 3 parts, child picks their pace"], ["4 · Lighthouse (8–9)", "Highlight off for 'My turn'; child taps each phrase as they finish it"]],
  feedback: "After 'My turn' the audience claps for every finished part; there is no score for reading aloud. The check question uses the usual \"Good guess, but try again\" and re-plays the line.",
  rationale: "Repeated, supported reading of the same text in phrases. The game does not judge reading aloud (no microphone scoring), so it practises fluency without claiming to measure it.",
  transfer: "Reading a part in a family play; reading a favourite page several times with expression.",
  a11y: ["Pace slider for the highlight", "Optional recording for a grown-up to listen back (off by default)", "Large text, wide line spacing"],
  visuals: ["Theatre stage with curtains", "Puppets", "Script card with phrase highlight", "Listen / Together / My turn buttons", "Audience that claps"],
  reward: { icon: "🎭", name: "A curtain call" },
  prompt: "My turn: read your line with the light.",
  correctLine: "Yes! The cat sat on the mat.", retryLine: "Good guess, but try again", doneLine: "Take a bow! The show is over.",
  scene: () => `<div class="script"><span class="ph on">The cat sat</span> <span class="ph">on a big red mat.</span></div><div class="row tight"><span class="chip">Listen</span><span class="chip">Together</span><span class="chip on">My turn</span></div><div class="q">Who sat on the mat?</div>` + row(O(P("🐱"), "ans card sm"), O(P("🐶"), "miss card sm")),
